{{smaller block|Than beginneth he to remember his life, and from that he falleth to thinke vpon his death. . . . And then beginneth he to thinke, that it were good to make sure, . . . least there hap to be suche blacke ''bugges'' indede as folke cal diuelles, whose tormentes he was wont to take for Poets tales.
